= Consensus mechanism — Simple =

A consensus mechanism is how a distributed system agrees on a shared valid state or history. Different mechanisms use different rules and assumptions. Consensus is more specific than simply taking a majority vote.

'''Important boundary:''' consensus mechanism ≠ majority vote.

== Sources ==
* NIST IR 8202, ''Blockchain Technology Overview'' (2018).
* NIST CSRC glossary, “Consensus model”: process to achieve agreement within a distributed system on the valid state.
